<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02365</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>41d8bdad-3304-4834-905e-b44988742bf0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>For the expressions in questions 1 – 4, choose which number would make the expression a perfect square. Then, choose an equivalent expression in factored form.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+3x\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>What number can be added to make \(x^2+3x\) a perfect square?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(\frac23\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac49\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac94\) </item>
  <item> \(-\frac23\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac94\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2+3x\)?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x(x + 3)\) </item>
  <item> \(x(3x)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 3)(x + 3)\) </item>
  <item> \(3(x + 1)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x(x + 3)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+0.6x\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What number can be added to make \(x^2+0.6x\) a perfect square?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 0.09 </item>
  <item> 0.81 </item>
  <item> 0.36 </item>
  <item> 0.03 </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0.09</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2+0.6x\)?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(
    x(x+0.6x)\) </item>
  <item> \(x(x+0.6)\) </item>
  <item> \(x(0.6x)\) </item>
  <item> \(0.6(x+1)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x(x+0.6)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2-11x\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>What number can be added to make \(x^2-11x\) a perfect square?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(\frac{11}{2}\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{25}{2}\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac52\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{121}{4}\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{121}{4}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2-11x\)?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x(x-11x)\) </item>
  <item> \(x(x-11)\) </item>
  <item> \(11(x-1)\) </item>
  <item> \(11x(x-1)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x(x-11)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What number can be added to make \(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\) a perfect square?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(\frac{25}{4}\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{25}{16}\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac58\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac68\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{25}{16}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\)?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x(x-\frac52)\) </item>
  <item> \(x(x-\frac{5}{2}x)\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{5}{2}x(x-1)\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{5}{2}(x-1)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x(x-\frac52)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>What number can be added to make \(x^2+x\) a perfect square?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(\frac14\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac12\) </item>
  <item> 1 </item>
  <item> 0 </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac14\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>What number can be added to make \(x^2-\frac{3}{2}x\) a perfect square?  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(\frac23\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac49\) </item>
  <item> \(\frac{9}{16}\) </item>
  <item> \(-\frac23\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{9}{16}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Noah is solving the equation \(x^2+8x+15=3\). He begins by rewriting the expression on the left in factored form and writes \((x+3)(x+5)=3\). He does not know what to do next. </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Do you think using the factored form is the best way for Noah to solve this equation?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Yes </item>
  <item> No </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> No</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the original equation, then choose the<emphasis> two</emphasis> roots.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(x = -4\) </item>
  <item>\(x = 12\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -2\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -6\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -2\), \(x = -6\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>An equation and its solutions are given. Solve the equation by completing the square, then choose whether you agree or disagree with the given solutions.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+20x+50=14\). The solutions are \(x=-18\) and \(x=2\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Agree </item>
  <item> Disagree </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Agree. The correct solutions are \(x=-18\) and \(x=2\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+1.6x=0.36\). The solutions are \(x=-1.8\) and \(x=0.2\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Agree </item>
  <item> Disagree </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Agree. \(x=-1.8\) and \(x=0.2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2-5x=\frac{11}{4}\). The solutions are \(x=\frac{11}{4}\) and \(x=-12\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Agree </item>
  <item> Disagree </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Disagree. The correct solutions are \(x=\frac{11}{2}\) and \(x=-\frac12\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item> Solve each equation, then choose the <emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2-0.5x=0.5\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = -0.5\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 1\) </item>
  <item>\( x = 0\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 2\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -1\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -0.5\), \(x = 1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+0.8x=0.09\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(x = -0.9\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 0.8\)</item>
  <item> \(x = 0.4\)</item>
  <item> \(x = 0.1\)</item>
  <item> \(x = 0.81\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -0.9\), \(x = 0.1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+\frac{13}{3}x=\frac{56}{36}\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = \frac{28}{3}\) </item>
  <item> \(x =\frac{1}{9}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=\frac{112}{36}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-\frac{14}{3}\) </item>
  <item> \(x = \frac13\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-\frac{14}{3}\), \(x=\frac13\)</para></section>
